  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "Both are correct. `legacy.mjs` is untouched and `dispatch` no longer routes through legacy.\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the route resolution in the request entry point by editing two writable files:\n\n### `registry.mjs` — `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)`\nThe original implementation had three bugs:\n1. **Wrong precedence**: it returned the first matching record in declaration order, so the dynamic `/users/:id` beat the static `/users/new`.\n2. **Fallback too eager**: it returned a fallback the moment it was encountered, even if a later static/dynamic record would match.\n3. **Weak validation**: a non-string path would throw an incidental error rather than a deliberate `TypeError`.\n\nThe rewrite now:\n- Validates the path up front: throws `TypeError` unless it's a string, nonempty, and starts with `/`.\n- Scans all records, remembering the **first** matching dynamic result and the **first** fallback, while returning immediately on the **first** static match (so any static wins over any dynamic, regardless of order).\n- Returns the dynamic match if no static matched, then the fallback, then `null`.\n- Never mutates records and builds fresh `params` objects per call.\n\n### `entry.mjs` — `dispatch(path)`\nRemoved the `legacyResolve` call so the production entry point uses only the production route table (`defaultRoutes`) via `resolveFromRegistry`. Validation and matching policy are inherited from the resolver.\n\n### Left unchanged (as required)\n- `legacy.mjs` — `legacyResolve` and its `/old/help` behavior are untouched; it remains a separate compatibility API.\n- `routes/static.mjs`, `routes/dynamic.mjs`, `routes/fallback.mjs` — already correct for the spec (exact static match; whole-segment nonempty dynamic params with original values; fresh fallback params).\n- `fixtures/routes.mjs`, adapters, and utilities — no changes needed.\n\nVerified against the public tests: `/users/new` → `user-new` (static beats earlier dynamic), `/users/Ada` → `user-detail` with `{id:'Ada'}`, `/missing` → `not-found`, `/health` via HTTP adapter → `health`, and `resolveFromRegistry('/x', [])` → `null`.",
